    "transparent_background": true,
    "prompt": "Create a production RPG sprite texture atlas by EDITING reference image 1. Reference 1 is a rigid 4 column x 6 row grid, 24 cells each exactly 256x256, total 1024x1536. Reference 2 defines the already approved soft clean hand-painted fantasy map style. Keep the exact 4x6 grid, exact canvas and cell geometry; no borders, labels, text, tile gaps or extra objects.\n\nCRITICAL: output REAL TRANSPARENCY. REMOVE THE FLAT GRASS BACKGROUND FROM EVERY CELL. Paint only the original visible object forms as RGBA cutouts, including the green objects even where their original palette resembles the grass. No grass rectangle, no checkerboard painted into RGB, no matte, no added background. Original game alpha will be restored separately by compositing over the existing grass.\n\nRepaint each original object, keeping its exact silhouette position, extent, center, clipping at the edges of its OWN cell, color family, dominant light/dark structure and overlap order. Do not center or shrink clipped objects. A shape cropped by a cell boundary must remain cropped there. Do not move anything between cells. Preserve all green conical/rounded foreground volumes and brown bases, particularly cells 0,8,12,13,19,20,21 (zero based row-major). Cell0 and cell12 have a green pointed object IN FRONT OF a cropped broad blue crown, retain both and the overlap. Blue and red shapes remain blue and red. Do not invent flowers, weapons, signs, extra branches, architectural details or new materials.\n\nPaint clear broad softly shaded masses with low surface noise, natural varied brushwork and soft rounded lighting, matching reference2. Render actual volume with smooth curves and restrained planes rather than pixel stair steps, outlines or individual tiny leaf/needle texture. This is high resolution hand-painted art, not enlarged pixel art, not photographic and not 3D plastic. The light green shapes in the original are foreground objects, NOT empty grass. The isolated brown and blue-gray forms in rows1-2 must keep their original small size, irregular shape and position; do not turn them into elaborate structures. For ambiguous shapes, preserve exactly the visible forms and color rather than inventing an identity.\n\nCell layout row-major (zero-based):\nrow0: blue cropped crown with tall green foreground; small irregular brown cluster at upper-middle; tiny flat brown fragment toward right half; tiny brown fragment at upper right.\nrow1: vertical narrow brown irregular form at center-right; broad small tan brown cluster; low blue-gray irregular cluster; large brown forked vertical form cropped at top.\nrow2: low green cone over brown base; narrow blue pointed crown; blue pointed crown variant; blue rounded crown with brown base cropped at top.\nrow3: blue broad crown cropped at top with green foreground; light green cone volume; large red pointed crown; blue pointed crown variant.\nrow4: broad blue rounded crown and brown base cropped at top; narrow red pointed crown; red rounded crown and brown base cropped at top; tall light green cone.\nrow5: dark green rounded crown with brown base cropped at top; light green rounded crown with brown base cropped at top; tall ivory beige pointed form; tall brown pointed form.\nDo not fill transparent space with extra objects. Output only the exact 1024x1536 atlas with alpha.",
